            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;line-height:1.45;margin:12px 14px}h2{font-size:15px;margin:14px 0 2px}h2:first-of-type{margin-top:0}h3{font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;opacity:.6;margin:10px 0 2px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:2px 0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,monospace}</style>
<h2>0.35.1</h2>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>This Mac says how many repositories need attention, not how many it serves</li>
</ul>
<h2>0.35.0</h2>
<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
<li>Storage shows what your devboxes take on disk</li>
</ul>
<h2>0.34.0</h2>
<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
<li>A devbox can be given a time to live</li>
<li>A devbox's page shows how to reach it over SSH</li>
<li>Choose which repository new devboxes are made from</li>
<li>This Mac shows the VM a devbox holds</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>Setup says a Mac can serve several repositories</li>
</ul>
<h2>0.33.0</h2>
<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
<li>A devbox greets you over SSH too</li>
<li>A devbox is called inside what you called it</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>This Mac's page stays put while the daemon restarts</li>
</ul>
<h2>0.32.1</h2>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>After an update the daemon is restarted without a button flashing by</li>
<li>Ssh into a devbox connects</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
